  "notes": [
   "Parts are the same as step 1; nothing was added or dropped.",
   "Both boards use catalogue type arduino-nano-33-ble because it exposes A4/A5, 3V3 and GND1. The reader is the Nano 33 BLE Sense and the writer is a Nano 33 BLE. The I2C bus is SDA on A4 and SCL on A5.",
   "The image draws the two bus lines (A5 = SCL teal, A4 = SDA yellow) joined between the boards with a 4.7k pull-up from each line to the red 3V line. I built this on bb1: SCL strip 5t, SDA strip 8t, 3V3 rail tp.1 to tp.3 (all one rail strip). r1 pulls SCL up and r2 pulls SDA up. The 3V3 comes only from the reader board, as in the image. The exact hole positions are my choice.",
   "GND is a direct jumper (wire1) between the GND1 pins of the two boards, as the image shows.",
   "Both boards are powered and programmed over USB from the computer (usb1, usb2). I gave these only a joined edge with no electrical edge, since the USB cable's ports are not modelled.",
   "bb2 is in the parts list but the image shows no connections to it, so it has no edges. The boards are drawn standalone with wires to their pins, so I did not mount them on breadboards.",
   "Only 6 jumper wires are used, as the image shows. The parts list's 10 is a pack quantity."
